    <h2>About</h2>
    <p>
        I am a Clinical Assistant Professor of Economics at Kennesaw State University. I completed my PhD in 
        Economics at the University of Notre Dame. As a research faculty member with Kennesaw State's Education Economics Center and
        Education Choice Research Lab, I study topics related to school finance, the K-12 teacher labor force, 
        and the school choice policy space more broadly.
    </p>
    
   
